  "notes": [
    {
      "segment": 1,
      "coptic_form": "ⲧ†ⲉ ⲛ̄ⲟ̄ⲓⲛⲣ̄ⲃⲁⲗ ⲁⲃⲁⲗ",
      "decision": "Rendered 'the Five Goings-Forth Out.' ⲟ̄ⲓⲛ- is the Lycopolitan action-noun prefix (= ⲧⲟⲓⲛ-) on ⲣ̄-ⲃⲁⲗ ⲁⲃⲁⲗ 'go forth out.' This chapter enumerates the cosmic redemptive going-forths of the Light.",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
    {
      "segment": 6,
      "coptic_form": "ⲧⲟ̄ⲓⲛ†ⲟⲩⲱ",
      "decision": "Translated 'the raising,' preserving the upward semantics of ⲧⲟⲩⲱ per terminology principles. The ⲟ̄ⲓⲛ- prefix substantivizes the verb. Paired here with ⲧⲟ̄ⲓⲛⲛⲟⲩϩⲙⲉ 'the saving,' giving the standard Manichaean dyad: raising-up + saving-out.",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
    {
      "segment": 19,
      "coptic_form": "ⲉⲧⲁⲩⲁⲙⲕϩ",
      "decision": "Translated 'whom they swallowed' — taking ⲁⲙⲕϩ as a Lycopolitan reduction/variant of ⲱⲙⲕ̄ 'swallow' (with -ϩ termination). The Manichaean cosmology of First Man being swallowed by darkness fits this register. Alternative ⲁⲙⲁϩⲧⲉ 'seize' is also possible.",
      "confidence": "moderate"
    },
    {
      "segment": 4,
      "coptic_form": "ⲡⲟⲩⲁⲓⲛⲉ ⲛⲟⲩϩⲙⲉ",
      "decision": "Read as 'the Light has-been-saved' with ⲛⲟⲩϩⲙⲉ as the qualitative state-form of ⲛⲁϩⲙ̄. The First Going-Forth narrative concerns the rescue of the Light captive within the archons.",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
    {
      "segment": 36,
      "coptic_form": "ⲛ̄ⲟⲓⲛⲛⲟⲩⲍⲙⲉ",
      "decision": "Translated 'salvation' (verbal-noun of ⲛⲁⲍⲙⲉϩ 'save/rescue', already in vocabulary). The ⲟⲓⲛ- prefix nominalizes the verbal stem to give an action-noun; this is the same structure as ⲧⲟⲓⲛⲃⲱⲗ 'the dissolution.' The series of 'salvations' (second, fourth, fifth) structures this kephalaion as an enumeration of cosmic redemptive acts.",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
    {
      "segment": 37,
      "coptic_form": "ⲧⲍⲱⲛⲏ",
      "decision": "Greek ζώνη 'girdle, zone' — the cosmological belt/zodiacal zone, already in accumulated vocabulary. Jesus the Radiance reveals himself in this Zone before the firmaments.",
      "confidence": "certain"
    },
    {
      "segment": 39,
      "coptic_form": "ⲡⲁⲣⲭⲓⲁⲕ...ⲭⲏ",
      "decision": "Reading uncertain across the line break. The word begins ⲡⲁⲣⲭⲓⲁⲕ- (with [ⲡⲁⲣⲭⲓⲁ] restored, ⲕ visible) and resumes ⲭⲏ on line 21. Possibilities include ⲁⲣⲭⲓⲉⲣⲁⲣⲭⲏ 'archhierarchy', ⲁⲣⲭⲓⲁ + ⲕⲁⲑⲟⲗⲓⲕⲏ 'catholic principle/origin', or some other Greek-derived ecclesiastical compound. Translated tentatively as 'arch-...-y' with the gap externalized. Jesus's establishment of this 'principle of all the churches' fits the Manichaean role of Jesus as founder of the apostolic line.",
      "confidence": "low"
    },
    {
